% Scope: one scenario straight_single; three interventions NOMINAL, THRUST_PULSE, THRUST_RATE_LIMIT; 0.025 s; 161 samples for 0--4 s. Existing MATLAB code not modified. First two previous V23 runs had fileread failure; V24 succeeded for all three diagnostic experiments.
% Mass: controller m_L=0.01 kg is R193_INITIAL_EKF_NOT_CURRENT, plant m_L=0.14 kg. No live EKF; cannot conclude latest estimate. Nominal mode uses clipped HLC commands, not necessarily unrestricted controller.
% Baseline NOMINAL: max |raw tau|=0.002133766 Nm; max position error=0.21849194 m; h first negative at t=3.000 s; min h=-0.0570164 at t=3.250. Hence completed diagnostic, not safety success.
% THRUST_PULSE: +3.3 N applied during 2.15<=t<2.35 s. First mismatch t=2.15. max |raw tau|=0.33947895 Nm at t=2.375; at the same time ||alpha2||=484.33055; Beta2 rcond=0.011054 and condition number=90.47; max position error=0.113872 m; min h=-0.0598274 at t=3.175. A single short pulse does not reproduce the earlier V19 R1 135.23 Nm; detailed V19 CBF intervention waveform/feedback must be replayed.
% THRUST_RATE_LIMIT: artificial +/-3 N/s limiter, NOT a tested motor model and NOT R2-1/-2/-3. First mismatch at 0.025 s (8.279 N raw vs 7.648 N applied); position error >5 cm at t=0.300 s; |raw tau|>1 Nm at t=1.200 s (2.46 Nm, Beta2 rcond ~0.109); first Beta2 rcond <1e-8 at t=2.925 s. Max |raw tau|=15069.918 Nm at t=2.925 s, ||alpha2||=1.0845096e16, rcond=3.095e-10, sigmaMin=222.92, sigmaMax=7.206e11, cable tilt ~89.71 deg, position error=3.66 m. Here the huge condition number is driven by very large sigmaMax, not sigmaMin approaching zero. Both alpha2 growth and ill-conditioning exist; neither implies all earlier torque rises were due to singular inverse. Max position error=16.468 m at 4 s; far outside normal flight.
% Isolation: Position error alone is not enough: NOMINAL 21.8 cm error with tiny torque; pulse case 5.4 cm error when torque 0.339 Nm. Probe results show instantaneous velocity, cable-angular-rate and attitude perturbations affect the alpha2 and torque at given fixed states; probes are not physical multi-step trajectories and cannot be compared as dimensionless sensitivity ranking across perturbation units.
% Common model: no synthetic random disturbances added; plant mass uses 0.14 kg, HLC fixed mhat=0.01 kg. Validity/physical constraints: safe cable-ellipsoid h becomes negative even in NOMINAL; this HLC-only test does not solve CBF constraints. Tension stayed positive in these diagnostics, but that is not proof of collision avoidance or flight safety.
% What this establishes: sustained thrust-command mismatch can precede tracking error, alpha2 growth and larger torque requests; extreme late failure coincides with an almost-horizontal cable and numerically badly conditioned Beta2. The exact causal chain of V19 135.23 Nm has NOT yet been reproduced or proven. Neither the HLC architecture nor Beta2 inverse alone can be declared faulty from these logs.
