% Isolation: Position error alone is not enough: NOMINAL 21.8 cm error with tiny torque; pulse case 5.4 cm error when torque 0.339 Nm. Probe results show instantaneous velocity, cable-angular-rate and attitude perturbations affect the alpha2 and torque at given fixed states; probes are not physical multi-step trajectories and cannot be compared as dimensionless sensitivity ranking across perturbation units.
% Common model: no synthetic random disturbances added; plant mass uses 0.14 kg, HLC fixed mhat=0.01 kg. Validity/physical constraints: safe cable-ellipsoid h becomes negative even in NOMINAL; this HLC-only test does not solve CBF constraints. Tension stayed positive in these diagnostics, but that is not proof of collision avoidance or flight safety.
% What this establishes: sustained thrust-command mismatch can precede tracking error, alpha2 growth and larger torque requests; extreme late failure coincides with an almost-horizontal cable and numerically badly conditioned Beta2. The exact causal chain of V19 135.23 Nm has NOT yet been reproduced or proven. Neither the HLC architecture nor Beta2 inverse alone can be declared faulty from these logs.
