% 【位置づけ】ユーザー提示V28結果ZIP（CBF_HLC_ROOTCAUSE_V28_20261117_114558_218.zip）に基づく設計検討。新MATLABコードの実装・実行は本追記では行っていない。V28以前の全累積引継ぎは上記にそのまま保持。
% 
% 1. V28で観測された事実
% NOMINAL: max raw |tau|=0.002134 Nm、3.000s完了。R1_EXACT: max=135.229437 Nm、2.350s R1_FILTER_STOP_INFEASIBLE_SHARED_THRUST。R1_BLEND_025: max 0.017884 Nm、2.750s INITIAL_RECTIFIED_SET_INVALID; R1_BLEND_050: max 16.764915 Nm、2.650s同失敗; R1_BLEND_075: max128.120635 Nm、2.350s推力不可行。ブレンドは正規CBFではなく、R1不等式のサンプル違反はそれぞれ24、20、8件。
% R1 + pitch +0.05Nm: 最大1389.259998 Nm、pitch -0.05Nm: 最大46.571568 Nm。roll +0.05Nm:129.174766 Nm、yaw +0.05Nm:135.238447 Nm。全て他の入力制約でクリップしており、新しいCBFとして安全を証明したわけではない。
% V19-R1 replay: 94 shared samples; max rawT diff 1.479382e-7 N; max raw torque inf diff 4.64e-5 Nm; max position error difference 4.093676e-11 m; V11_19限定。
% R1 2.150s: applied T12.172245N vs raw8.867666N、raw torque0.001596Nm, posErr0.040584m, velErr0.076726m/s。2.175s: raw torque0.088193Nm、velErr0.117029m/s、Vs norm125.171。2.275s: T 12.521498 vs raw2.849852N、raw torque1.679520Nm、velErr0.269860、Vs norm372.725。2.300s: T13.50173 vs raw0.415391N、raw torque135.229437Nm、posErr0.046482m、velErr0.367220m/s、Vs norm657.373、Beta2 cond4.226587、cable q_z=-0.997356。2.325s raw T=-2.722722N applied16.447536N, raw torque2.655445Nm, posErr0.050022m。
% Gain knockout at 2.300s R1: F2 x axis #3=111.599602 Nm, #4=37.170540 Nm, #5=22.612300 Nm in per-term difference; these numbers cannot simply be added as absolute magnitudes because signed cancellation and matrix map. All 23 sampled gain reconstructions PASS, max Vs reconstruction residual 2.273737e-13. F2#3 corresponds to x-horizontal second-derivative tracking quantity in generated Vs, not a stand-alone physical acceleration mismatch proof.
% IMPORTANT STOP-ROW CAVEAT: the R1_EXACT 2.350s row has R1FilterStoppedHere=1 and appliedThrust_N=0 by diagnostic fallback to clipped nominal while the filter has ALREADY declared infeasible, and NO plant step is applied. Its recorded tension0.001196N is NOT an executed CBF action. For physical min tension exclude stop/unapplied rows. At 2.325s (last applicable step) tension2.547682N.
% 
% 2. Fundamental distinctions for the user's new question
% (a) pointwise algebraic consistency: given x and invertible mapping, replacing the physical control by a virtual command consistent with the SAME physical u does not change the plant response at all. Renaming/reparameterizing a control is not a new stabilizing intervention. In the generated HLC, T=Uf(x,ref,v1) and tau=Beta2(x,ref,v1)^{-1} V2_alpha2(x,ref,v1-jets,vs). If T changes, re-evaluate Uf, Beta2, V2_alpha2; do NOT keep beta/alpha frozen from original v1. If beta/alpha are well-defined and affine in virtual variables, algebraic inverse can be checked with forward reconstruction residual.
% (b) jet/time consistency: v1, dv1, d2v1, d3v1, d4v1 are NOT five independent control variables without extra dynamics. A time-varying changed v1(t) must have derivatives consistent with its evolution; changing only v1 in each 25ms sample and holding higher jets from old reference is pointwise but NOT dynamically consistent. Smoothness and slew constraints; new HLC inversion must respect thrust and torque hard boxes with no silent saturation.
% (c) reference/error consistency: even perfect inversion of a modified virtual input forces a NEW output behavior. The original trajectory may become temporarily unreachable. The unchanged high-gain HLC feedback can demand huge actions, or the actuator box/safety set may make commands infeasible; algebraic consistency alone does not prevent this.
% (d) actual plant/sensor consistency: controller estimated load mhat, plant true mL, physical actuation, sample-and-hold and state estimates differ. A virtual inverse constructed with mhat need not produce the claimed output derivative in true plant. Match and verify this residual in original 3D plant with and without EKF, not an invented EKF value.
% 
% 3. Priority test matrix (same plant/trajectory/initial states/mhat/input limits)
% A NOMINAL: raw HLC then physical clipping, log before/after.
% B R1_DIRECT: genuine R1 CBF recomputed each 25ms, physical thrust corrected, torque nominal/clipped (V19/V28 reproduction).
% C R1_REINVERT_POINTWISE: choose R1's same thrust correction; invert Uf with a modified v1 and recompute Vs, Beta2, V2_alpha2 and physical torques at same state. Hold higher v1 jets nominal ONLY as an intentionally labeled algebraic diagnostic; verify input bounds and residual; not an honest dynamically consistent virtual controller and not safe automatically.
% D R1_VIRTUAL_JET_CONSISTENT: use a realizable, differentiable virtual command/jet, project through exact generated HLC, enforce actual T/tau limits; reconstruct & verify derivative coherence at successive 25ms steps and one-step physical plant. If no feasible candidate, STOP_INFEASIBLE; never clip and label it mapping-consistent.
% E SAME_PHYSICAL_INPUT_DIFFERENT_DESCRIPTION (null test): physical u exactly B, only calculate equivalent virtual representation; state trajectory and HLC outputs must match B to solver/integrator tolerance. This confirms algebraic relabeling alone cannot improve behavior.
% F TORQUE_ONLY and THRUST_ONLY and JOINT: single-step and sustained interventions, equal matched magnitude/limits, compare virtual residual/closed loop.
% G WITH_VS_WITHOUT_VS_OUTER_FEEDBACK: diagnostic gain term cancellation at fixed state, NOT an approved alternate flight controller or 'gain tuning success'. Need causal comparison of second derivative tracking errors, derivative levels, and cancellation.
% H SATURATION_ONLY: branch at 2.275s into physical tau box and artificially unbounded torque for 25/50ms, label the unbounded run NONPHYSICAL, to isolate saturation as cause/amplifier. Never count nonphysical case as avoidance success.
% I MASS & MODEL: mhat=0.01 initial replay separately from live EKF estimates; true plant mL=0.14 only plant; 19-state vs original 24-state parity, high-order derivative consistency; no oracle mass in controller.
% J INTERSAMPLE & HARD CONSTRAINTS: preserve cable ellipsoid h, all physical input bounds, positive cable tension, sample/hold 25ms plus substeps; record CBF residual and feasibility, do NOT silence failed safety rows.
% 
% 4. Metrics & interpretation
% Log rawHLC 4 inputs, clipped nominal, proposed CBF, finally applied, achieved next state, HLC fully reconstructed tau, Uf residual, beta/alpha, singular values, D=qz(q.b3), pL position/velocity error, reconstructed x-horizontal acceleration and jerk errors, Vs14 signed terms and cancellations; actual-vs-desired virtual-output derivative (if mathematically defined for the model), derivative/jet time consistency, mhat and true mass separated, hard-box feasibility, h and continuous sample approximations, cable tension at actually propagated steps; solver status/time.
% Report the earliest time when each event happens: intervention, derivative mismatch, first Vs surge, raw torque > physical box, actual torque clipping, HLC map condition warning, CBF infeasible, physical h violation. Differentiate algebraic exactness, causal paired test, and invariant safety proof. A large number in virtual mapping may be FEASIBILITY failure even if cable h remains positive.
% 
% 5. Literature touchpoints (not model-specific guarantees)
% Convens et al., IFAC-PapersOnLine 2017, Control of Fully Actuated Unmanned Aerial Vehicles with Actuator Saturation (feedback linearization, actuator saturation, reference governor), DOI 10.1016/j.ifacol.2017.08.1823.
% Design of shifting state-feedback controllers for constrained feedback linearized systems: Application to quadrotor attitude control, International Journal of Robust and Nonlinear Control (2023) DOI 10.1002/rnc.7098: physical constraints mapped into the virtual-input domain.
% These works are not directly applicable proofs for the present cable-suspended drone; refer to exact generated HLC and 3D plant.
% 
% 6. Engineering and deliverables
% Only one replaceable MATLAB .m at common_matlab root when implementing; use the existing common_matlab/_CBF_TEST_OUTPUT folder, create only if missing; save a single self-contained ZIP per run (CSV/plots/results/cumulative text). ZIP verification before deleting temporary working files. Do not generate detached source files. Preserve all old cumulative handover content. No program changes were made in the current V29 theoretical analysis.
% V30_FULL_V29_HANDOVER_END


% =========================================================================
% V32 ORIGINAL FLIGHT-GENERATED JET + CONTINUOUS NONLINEAR CLOSED-LOOP AUDIT
% User's unchanged R193 nominal generator: gen_ref_line(...), order=6,
% with the SLOAD payload Z shift ONCE on position, not its derivatives.
% This is NOT the complete Flight/EKF/replanner scheduler; original plant
% reproduction uses the existing CBF_V19_OriginalPlantStep adapter.
% =========================================================================
function S=v32ContinuousReferenceStudy(work,opts)
assert(strcmpi(opts.parameterSet,'R193'), 'CBF:HLCV32PhysicalSet', ...
 'V32 requires R193 true plant, cable length and controller parameter set');
if exist('gen_ref_line','file')~=2
 root=fileparts(mfilename('fullpath'));
 if isfolder(fullfile(root,'reference')),addpath(fullfile(root,'reference'));end
end
assert(exist('gen_ref_line','file')==2 && ...
 exist('gen_ref_for_rigid_body','file')==2, ...
 'CBF:HLCV32MissingOriginalGenerator', ...
 'Actual R193 gen_ref_line and gen_ref_for_rigid_body must be on MATLAB path. No synthetic fallback.');
raw=gen_ref_line('p0',[0,0,3],'velocity',1.5,'direction',[0,1,0]);
jetStruct=gen_ref_for_rigid_body(raw,6);
% R193 source actually returns a STRUCT with .pYaw, .q and .rotms;
% older V32 incorrectly expected the whole return value to be a handle.
assert(isstruct(jetStruct) && isfield(jetStruct,'pYaw') && ...
  isa(jetStruct.pYaw,'function_handle') && isfield(jetStruct,'order') ...
  && jetStruct.order>=6,'CBF:HLCV33JetStruct',...
  'R193 original gen_ref_for_rigid_body must provide struct.pYaw 6-jet');
jet=jetStruct.pYaw;
testJet=double(jet(0));testJet=testJet(:);
assert(numel(testJet)==28 && all(isfinite(testJet)),...
 'CBF:HLCV33JetShape','Original R193 .pYaw reference does not have 28 entries');
sc=CBF_V19_Scenarios('straight_single','R193');
sc.dt=opts.dt;sc.duration=opts.continuousDuration;
L=sc.settings.physical.cableLength;
base=@(t) v32FlightLoadJet(jet,t,L);
sc.refFull=base;sc.ref=@(t,k) v32XYZJet(base,t,k);
% User-owned Flight takeoff/phase transitions are NOT fabricated here.
% Diagnostic state is a prescribed steady-motion Flight-phase initial
% state. The real 24-state flight can additionally be started by a user-
% supplied actual 19-state equivalent snapshot from the same flight tick.
if ~isempty(opts.continuousInitialState19)
    assert(~any(abs([opts.continuousDiagnosticCableTiltDeg,...
       opts.continuousDiagnosticBodyRollDeg,...
       opts.continuousDiagnosticCableOmegaRadps,...
       opts.continuousDiagnosticLateralVelocityMps])>0),...
       'CBF:HLCV35SnapshotAndSynthetic',...
       'Do not combine an actual Flight snapshot with synthetic initial perturbations');
    xx=double(opts.continuousInitialState19(:));
    assert(numel(xx)==19&&all(isfinite(xx)), ...
        'CBF:HLCV32InitialState','Provide an actual finite 19-state Flight snapshot');
    sc.x0=xx;
    initSource='USER_SUPPLIED_FLIGHT_SNAPSHOT_19';
else
    xx=sc.x0;
    r=base(0);
    xx(8:10)=r(1:3);xx(11:13)=r(5:7);
    yaw=r(4);xx(1:4)=[cos(yaw/2);0;0;sin(yaw/2)];
    xx(14:16)=[0;0;-1];xx(17:19)=[0;0;0];
    % User-requested V35: distinguish post-HLC input changes from initial
    % off-manifold / unsatisfied-reference states. This optional controlled
    % perturbation is NOT a real Flight EKF snapshot.
    theta=opts.continuousDiagnosticCableTiltDeg*pi/180;
    roll=opts.continuousDiagnosticBodyRollDeg*pi/180;
    w=opts.continuousDiagnosticCableOmegaRadps;
    vx=opts.continuousDiagnosticLateralVelocityMps;
    assert(all(isfinite([theta,roll,w,vx])) && abs(theta)<pi/3 &&...
        abs(roll)<pi/3 && abs(w)<=2 && abs(vx)<=2,...
        'CBF:HLCV35InitialStateSettings',...
        'Diagnostic tilt/roll/omega/vx must be finite and within declared diagnostic bounds');
    if any(abs([theta,roll,w,vx])>1e-14)
      xx(14:16)=[0;sin(theta);-cos(theta)];
      xx(17:19)=[0;w*cos(theta);w*sin(theta)];
      xx(1:4)=[cos(roll/2);sin(roll/2);0;0];
      xx(11)=xx(11)+vx;
      initSource=sprintf('V35_DIAGNOSTIC_PHYSICAL_STATE_TILT_%.3gDEG_ROLL_%.3gDEG_OMEGA_%.3g_VX_%.3g',...
          opts.continuousDiagnosticCableTiltDeg,opts.continuousDiagnosticBodyRollDeg,w,vx);
    else
      initSource='DIAGNOSTIC_STEADY_MOTION_MATCHED_TO_R193_FLIGHT_NOMINAL';
    end
    sc.x0=xx;
end
% Ellipsoid center measured relative to the actual source's initial
% payload position and nominal direction (NOT the V19 artificial x-path).
p0=base(0); o=struct();o.type='ellipsoid';
o.center=[p0(1)+.28;p0(2)+2.5;p0(3)+L/2];
o.axes=[.28;.36;.55];
a=pi/5; o.R=[cos(a) -sin(a) 0;sin(a) cos(a) 0;0 0 1];
sc.obstacles={o};
initialH=v23CableSafety(sc.x0,sc);
assert(initialH>0,'CBF:HLCV32InitialObstacle', ...
 'The original-reference comparison starts with an unsafe cable ellipsoid h=%g',initialH);
rows=cell(0,20);cases=v32CaseList(opts);
refAudit=v32ReferenceAudit(sc,base,opts,work);
try
 v34SmoothstepAudit(work,opts);
catch MEwave
 % The input-perturbation self-audit is diagnostic, not a reason to
 % suppress the true original-reference flight simulation.
 v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V34_SMOOTH_INPUT_WAVE_AUDIT_WARNING.txt'),...
    getReport(MEwave,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
end
try
 v33LocalJetOrderAudit(sc,opts,work);
 v35LocalSensitivityAudit(sc,opts,work);
catch MEjet
 v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V33_LOCAL_JET_ORDER_AUDIT_WARNING.txt'),...
  getReport(MEjet,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
end
try
 v35R1InitialFeasibilityAudit(sc,work);
catch MEr1
 v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V35_R1_INITIAL_GEOMETRY_WARNING.txt'),...
  getReport(MEr1,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
end
for j=1:size(cases,1)
    caseID=cases{j,1};profile=cases{j,2};mode=cases{j,3};
    current=sc;
    if strcmp(profile,'C7_LANE_FAST') || strcmp(profile,'C7_LANE_SLOW')
        if strcmp(profile,'C7_LANE_FAST'),D=opts.continuousFastRamp;
        else,D=opts.continuousSlowRamp;end
        orig=base;
        current.refFull=@(t)v32LaneFullJet(orig,t,opts.continuousLaneOffset,...
            opts.continuousLaneStart,D,opts.continuousLaneHold);
        thisReference=current.refFull;
        current.ref=@(t,k)v32XYZJet(thisReference,t,k);
    end
    localOpts=v37ConfigureMode(opts,mode);
    fprintf('[HLC V37] %s | %s | %s | dV1=%.4g Vs=[%.4g %.4g %.4g] rise=%.3g\n',...
        caseID,profile,mode,localOpts.continuousV1Amplitude,...
        localOpts.v37DeltaVs(:),localOpts.continuousV1Rise);
    try
        [tr,sm]=v32RunContinuousOne(current,mode,localOpts);
        writetable(tr,fullfile(work,['v32_trace_' lower(caseID) '.csv']));
        if opts.makePlots && ~isempty(tr)
            v32Plot(tr,work,caseID);
        end
        rows(end+1,:)={caseID,profile,mode,initSource,...
            sm.status,sm.detail,sm.tEnd,sm.maxRawTau,sm.maxRawT,...
            sm.maxPosErr,sm.maxVs,sm.minH,sm.minTension,...
            sm.nHnegative,sm.nClip,sm.maxMapResidual,sm.maxJetDemand,...
            sm.firstClip,sm.firstHnegative,sm.maxAppliedMismatch}; %#ok<AGROW>
    catch ME
        v23WriteText(fullfile(work,['V32_ERROR_' caseID '.txt']), ...
            getReport(ME,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
        rows(end+1,:)={caseID,profile,mode,initSource,...
            ['MATLAB_ERROR_' ME.identifier],ME.message,...
            NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN,NaN}; %#ok<AGROW>
    end
    v32WriteCaseSummary(rows,work);
end
statuses=string(rows(:,5));
S=struct('nCases',size(rows,1),...
 'nRuntimeErrors',sum(startsWith(statuses,'MATLAB_ERROR_')),...
 'nR1FilterStops',sum(startsWith(statuses,'R1_FILTER_STOP_')),...
 'nFailedCases',sum(statuses~='COMPLETED_DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_SAFETY_CERTIFIED'));
if any(strcmpi(char(opts.continuousProfile),{'coupled','coupled_full'}))
 try
  v37WriteDetailedResults(work,rows,opts);
 catch MEv37
  v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V37_AUDIT_ERROR.txt'),...
    getReport(MEv37,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
 end
 try
  v38WriteVirtualChannelAudit(work,rows,opts);
 catch MEv38
  v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V38_VIRTUAL_RELATION_AUDIT_ERROR.txt'),...
    getReport(MEv38,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
 end
end
% Compare the two labels that MUST yield identical physical inputs.
% A difference is a bug or a rank/clip event, not a stability benefit.
try
 if ~any(strcmpi(char(opts.continuousProfile),{'coupled','coupled_full'}))
  v33ComparePhysicalEquivalence(work,rows);
 end
catch MEequiv
 v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V36_TORQUE_EQUIVALENCE_WARNING.txt'), ...
   getReport(MEequiv,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
end
try
 if ~strcmpi(char(opts.continuousProfile),'coupled')
  v35CompareV1DerivativeModes(work,rows);
 end
catch MEv35
 v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V35_DERIVATIVE_CLOSED_LOOP_COMPARISON_WARNING.txt'),...
   getReport(MEv35,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
end
note={...
 'SOURCE: Original R193 run_flight_headless nominal gen_ref_line p0 [0 0 3], 1.5m/s, +Y. gen_ref_for_rigid_body order 6; SLOAD subtract cableL once from payload Z position.';...
 'V33 runs a continuous sequential nonlinear closed loop, 25ms input updates, 4 RK substeps. Original R193_24 plant adapter by default, or explicit 19-state alternative.';...
 'DIAGNOSTIC STEADY-MOTION INITIAL STATE is NOT the recorded post-takeoff original Flight state. Provide opts.continuousInitialState19 for a measured snapshot.';...
 'V34 DEFAULT uses ONLY R193 original normal constant-speed straight 6-jet. C7 and replan are OFF unless explicitly opted in.';...
 'NOMINAL and C7_LANE change only reference; POST_V1_T changes only applied thrust; V1_VALUE and V1_JET recompute torque using generated HLC inverse map.';...
 'Same input in different labels gives the same plant evolution. Incremental V1_JET d0..4 is time-consistent; native generated Vfd is NOT proved to be a physical continuous-time derivative jet.';...
 'A 6th-derivative continuous reference does not guarantee input feasibility, safety, or HLC-domain validity. Controller estimated mass is not a live EKF unless user explicitly supplies an EKF trace.';...
 'CBF R1_EXACT is the earlier thrust-only rectified filter, re-evaluated from current state each cycle; it can stop as infeasible. No R2 or virtual 4-DOF safety controller is certified in V32.';...
 'Raw demanded virtual map vs physically clipped commands are separately logged; a clipping event fails the physical mapping consistency test, even if the unclipped algebraic residual is zero.';...
 'Obstacles use the existing cable outer ellipsoid versus one rotated static ellipsoid; no protection sphere or ground CBF is added.';...
 'The R193 true physical 0.14kg and the fixed initial EKF estimate 0.01kg are deliberately different. No true mass is substituted into HLC.';...
 'V33: Original gen_ref_for_rigid_body returns struct.pYaw function, corrected. Torque direct vs mapped virtual is pointwise algebraic equivalence only, not continuous 6-jet coherence. V1 derivative subset 0..4 and torque + V1 joint are tested. Substep h/tension are sampled, not formally certified.'};
try
 v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V34_README_AND_INTERPRETATION.txt'),strjoin(note,newline));
catch MEnote
 v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V36_README_WARNING.txt'), ...
   getReport(MEnote,'extended','hyperlinks','off'));
end
assert(refAudit,'CBF:HLCV32ReferenceAudit','Original/C7 reference derivative audit failed');
end

