% Append full history AFTER simulation. Never block the plant on a
% nonphysical string-length threshold.
v36WriteHandover(work,root,opts);
p=fullfile(work,'CBF_CUMULATIVE_HANDOVER_V36.txt');
assert(isfile(p),'CBF:HLCV37HandoverAbsent','V36 history file absent');
prior=fileread(p);
assert(contains(prior,'V34 ADDENDUM') && contains(prior,'V35 ADDENDUM')...
 && contains(prior,'V36 ADDENDUM'), 'CBF:HLCV37HandoverMarkers',...
 'Prior cumulative appendices absent');
add=[newline newline ...
 '===== V37 ADDENDUM 2026-11-17: continuous corrected virtual four-channel input, amplitudes and timing =====' newline ...
 'Observed user V35 ZIP CBF_HLC_ROOTCAUSE_V35_20261117_134918_281.zip: ONLY ERROR_TOP_LEVEL.txt plus cumulative V34 txt; HLC V35 flight DID NOT RUN. v35WriteHandover at line 13019 incorrectly rejects a real Japanese UTF8 cumulative string with the numel(prior)>250000 threshold. Removed numeric threshold, preserved previous addenda marker checks and deferred all history creation until AFTER main simulations (V36 approach). No claim made about V35 model performance.' newline ...
 'User rightly demands a CONTINUOUS closed-loop comparison, not a frozen state or mere relabeling. Same unmodified R193 source regular 6-jet straight target; case-by-case applied physical corrections are recomputed at every 25ms sample and reintegrated with original nonlinear plant and exact HLC generated maps. All cases share initial physical state, controller estimated mass and static cable ellipsoid obstacle.' newline ...
 'V37 coupled quick: C01 NOMINAL; C02 POST_T altered virtual v1 thrust but stale HLC torque; C03 NATIVE_V1 corrected v1 analytic derivatives 0..4 and recomputed torque; C04 NATIVE_ALL corrected v1 and smooth delta v2-v4, generated full 4D real input; C05 POST_SAME_ALL exact physical 4D identity control; C06 POST_INDEPENDENT altered thrust plus unrelated physical torque offset; C07 POST_TAU torque only; C08 NATIVE_VS altered v2-v4 alone; C09 R1_EXACT (may be immediately infeasible, not claimed continuous CBF). Coupled_full adds low/high amplitudes and slow rise/fall, x/y/yaw virtual-channel corrections, and the original value-only to derivative-order-4 hierarchy as C23..C28.' newline ...
 'V37 output V37_CONTINUOUS_CORRECTION_METRICS.csv and V37_MATCHED_CLOSED_LOOP_PAIRS.csv; each 25ms trace contains virtual target thrust/torque, requested/applied deviations, altered Beta2 condition, v1 d0..4 increments, Vs increment, saturation, 4 RK substep h and tension. Cases stop on serious HLC domain/tension/nonfinite, with status; previous raw HLC max torque is distinct from corrected physical demand.' newline ...
 'V37 differentiates algebraic mapping from true closed-loop performance. Any same applied 4D input gives same dynamics; a corrected virtual trajectory may still cause HLC raw tracking commands and physical saturation to increase. Corrected virtual additions alone do not establish that ORIGINAL Vfd state feedback is a continuously correct time derivative jet. R1 can be infeasible at t=0, and no R2/real virtual CBF safety filter is certified.' newline ...
 'Default diagnostic tilt/omega state is synthetic not the user original Flight state; fixed initial EKF estimate of 0.01kg not live. Plant physical true load mass 0.14kg; physical bounds simulator assumptions. No additional file required in MATLAB installation; history remains embedded in this single source and archives to one ZIP.' newline];
v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'CBF_CUMULATIVE_HANDOVER_V37.txt'),[prior add]);
delete(p);
end



function dv=v38FullV1Wave(t,opts)
% Six generated native Vfd slots: v1(t), ..., d^5 v1/dt^5.
% The original R193 geometric closed-loop controller's own Vfd columns
% still are not proven to be the continuous derivative jet.
dv=zeros(1,6);start=opts.continuousV1Start;
for k=0:5
 dv(k+1)=opts.continuousV1Amplitude*(...
     v32S7(t-start,opts.continuousV1Rise,k)-...
     v32S7(t-(start+opts.continuousV1Rise+opts.continuousV1Hold),...
             opts.continuousV1Fall,k));
end
end

function v38WriteVirtualChannelAudit(work,R,opts)
% Every sample comes from a propagated nonlinear 19-state physical state,
% not from an isolated frozen-state evaluation. Native-vs-coupled-vs-added
% channels are deliberately kept separate. This is not a CBF certificate.
cols={'caseID','mode','time_s','deltaV1Value',...
 'deltaV1D1','deltaV1D2','deltaV1D3','deltaV1D4','deltaV1D5',...
 'coupledVsChangeInf','independentVsChangeInf','totalVsChangeInf',...
 'v2CoupledChange','v3CoupledChange','v4CoupledChange',...
 'extraV2','extraV3','extraV4',...
 'rawHLCTorqueInf_Nm','requestedTorqueInf_Nm','appliedTorqueInf_Nm',...
 'desiredToAppliedClipInf','betaRcond',...
 'pointwiseTargetThrustMismatch_N','pointwiseTargetTorqueMismatch_Nm'};
rows=cell(0,numel(cols));
jetCols={'caseID','mode','timeMid_s','order',...
    'nativeDerivativeTrapezoidMismatch',...
    'modifiedDerivativeTrapezoidMismatch',...
    'addedWaveDerivativeTrapezoidMismatch'};
jetRows=cell(0,numel(jetCols));
for jj=1:size(R,1)
 id=R{jj,1};mode=R{jj,3};
 f=fullfile(work,['v32_trace_' lower(id) '.csv']);
 if ~isfile(f),continue;end
 t=readtable(f);N=height(t);
 for k=1:N
  db=[t.v1CoupledV2(k)-t.nativeV2(k),...
      t.v1CoupledV3(k)-t.nativeV3(k),...
      t.v1CoupledV4(k)-t.nativeV4(k)];
  de=[t.independentDeltaV2(k),t.independentDeltaV3(k),...
      t.independentDeltaV4(k)];
  rows(end+1,:)={id,mode,t.time_s(k),...
   t.targetV1_D0(k)-t.nativeV1_D0(k),...
   t.targetV1_D1(k)-t.nativeV1_D1(k),...
   t.targetV1_D2(k)-t.nativeV1_D2(k),...
   t.targetV1_D3(k)-t.nativeV1_D3(k),...
   t.targetV1_D4(k)-t.nativeV1_D4(k),...
   t.targetV1_D5(k)-t.nativeV1_D5(k),...
   norm(db,Inf),norm(de,Inf),norm(db+de,Inf),...
   db(1),db(2),db(3),de(1),de(2),de(3),...
   t.HLC_rawTauInf_Nm(k),t.desiredTauInf_Nm(k),...
   t.appliedTauInf_Nm(k),t.desiredToAppliedClipInf(k),...
   t.alteredBetaRcond(k),...
   t.afterClipTargetThrustMismatch_N(k),...
   t.afterClipTargetTorqueMismatch_Nm(k)}; %#ok<AGROW>
 end
 for k=1:N-1
  dt=t.time_s(k+1)-t.time_s(k);
  if dt<=0,continue;end
  for order=0:4
   d0=sprintf('nativeV1_D%d',order);
   d1=sprintf('nativeV1_D%d',order+1);
   q0=sprintf('targetV1_D%d',order);
   q1=sprintf('targetV1_D%d',order+1);
   a0=t.(d0);a1=t.(d1);b0=t.(q0);b1=t.(q1);
   rn=(a0(k+1)-a0(k))/dt-.5*(a1(k)+a1(k+1));
   rm=(b0(k+1)-b0(k))/dt-.5*(b1(k)+b1(k+1));
   re=rm-rn;
   jetRows(end+1,:)={id,mode,.5*(t.time_s(k)+t.time_s(k+1)),...
      order,rn,rm,re}; %#ok<AGROW>
  end
 end
end
assert(size(rows,2)==numel(cols) && size(jetRows,2)==numel(jetCols),...
 'CBF:HLCV38AuditShape','Virtual channel output dimension mismatch');
writetable(cell2table(rows,'VariableNames',cols),...
 fullfile(work,'V38_V1_V234_COUPLING_EVERY_25MS.csv'));
writetable(cell2table(jetRows,'VariableNames',jetCols),...
 fullfile(work,'V38_V1_TIME_DERIVATIVE_CONSISTENCY.csv'));
notes={...
 'V38 CHANNEL AUDIT: v1 baseline and modified derivatives d0..5 are logged at every physical state. v234Coupled = original Vs(x,XD,newV1,P,F2,F3,F4). Independent extra deltaVs is logged separately. The actual candidate physical 4-input is computed using Uf(x,newV1), Beta2(x,newV1) and V2_alpha2(x,newV1,v234Coupled+deltaVs).';...
 'NATIVE_V1 (C03) changes the full six-component analytic incremental v1 jet (d0..5) AND RECOMPUTES the dependent v234 through Vs. NATIVE_ALL (C04) also applies independent changes to the three virtual channels. POST_T (C02) uses the same changed v1 thrust but keeps old physical torque. POST_SAME_ALL (C05) applies exactly the SAME real input as C04 and must reproduce its trajectory.';...
 'Time derivative audit covers d0 to d4 derivative relationships and reports the discrepancy between finite-differenced total v1[k] and the average of claimed derivative channels on consecutive ticks. It is a DIAGNOSTIC, not a mathematical differentiability proof. Native Vfd state-feedback derivative columns were NOT derived from the total closed-loop time derivative and can show mismatch.';...
 'No assumption that v2..v4 have to be numerically equal to a function of v1 only: for the load-position-yaw output choice they are independent controlled virtual-output channels. The dependency that MUST be recomputed when v1 changes is the original generated Vs(x,XD,v1,...) plus input mapping Uf/Beta2/alpha2. An independent deltaVs is a new commanded output acceleration and requires feasibility and time trajectory consistency checks.';...
 'Physical clipping breaks the requested virtual mapping. All cases use 25ms ZOH and nonlinear plant propagation on the unchanged normal R193 0..6 target; no rerouting/replanning target is inserted. The physical initial condition can be baseline or an explicitly provided real Flight snapshot.'};
v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'V38_VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_INTERPRETATION.txt'),...
 strjoin(notes,newline));
end

function v38WriteHandover(work,root,opts)
