v37WriteHandover(work,root,opts);
p=fullfile(work,'CBF_CUMULATIVE_HANDOVER_V37.txt');
assert(isfile(p),'CBF:HLCV38Handover','V37 accumulated handover missing');
prior=fileread(p);
assert(contains(prior,'V37 ADDENDUM') && contains(prior,'V36 ADDENDUM'),...
 'CBF:HLCV38History','Historical version markers missing');
notes={...
 '===== V38 ADDENDUM 2026-11-17: MATLAB V37 parse repair; natural 6-jet continuous virtual-channel relationship study =====';...
 'User V37 failure: MATLAB error at test_CBF_HLC_RootCause.m line 13343: reserved end used incorrectly. Source bug: last text concatenation line of v37WriteHandover erroneously contained newline ...];. MATLAB continuation (...) made the closing bracket invalid. V38 replaces it with newline];. This was source-syntax error before any simulation; V37 has NO measured flight result in that failed run.';...
 'User requests NORMAL repeated 25ms nonlinear simulation with unchanged original R193 regular 0..6 differentiable Flight target. No artificial retargeting and no requirement to use a tilted synthetic initial state; use default initial physical state. If the original equilibrium gives structurally zero v1 high-order torque coupling, use an actual recorded nondegenerate Flight snapshot when available and disclose any separately generated physical diagnostic state.';...
 'Crucial coupling: native Vfd is six-component d0..5; a complete incremental v1 jet requires modifying all SIX slots. The generated torque map may depend on lower orders, but the Vs relation still must be recomputed. Native v1 and its derivatives d0..5 do not suffice alone. The original HLC maps v234 = Vs(x,XD,v1,P,F2,F3,F4), with beta=Beta2(x,XD,v1,P), alpha=V2_alpha2(x,XD,v1,v234,P), and T=Uf(x,XD,v1,P). Any changed v1 requires recomputation of Vs/Beta2/alpha and the resulting real thrust/three torques; otherwise the post-HLC physical input need not satisfy the modified virtual target.';...
 'Additional independent delta(v2,v3,v4) is allowed as a virtual command to change the desired flat-output high-order accelerations; it is NOT automatically a derivatives-consistent reference, and must NOT be mislabeled as a fixed relation determined uniquely by v1. V38 logs base vs, Vs recomputed from modified v1, extra deltaVs, full target Vs and applied physical inputs separately EVERY 25ms in all V37 coupled variants.';...
 'V38_V1_TIME_DERIVATIVE_CONSISTENCY.csv checks native/modified v1 derivative-jet coherence through d4-to-d5 across subsequent time ticks using a trapezoid consistency residual; it is a numerical diagnostic at dt=0.025s, not proof, and the native Vfd high-order outputs may not equal derivatives along nonlinear feedback trajectories.';...
 'C02 POST_T, C03 NATIVE_V1, C04 NATIVE_ALL (now with d0..5 v1 changes, unlike legacy partial C23..C28), C05 same physical 4D input, C06 independent post torque, C07 torque-only, C08 altered virtual Vs, C09 R1 exact, plus magnitudes/time ramps and partial derivative orders C23..C28 in coupled_full. All use the SAME original target and states integrated sequentially. Case summaries distinguish runtime errors/early stops/safety failures; R1 may be unavailable from time zero; never claim CBF safety certification.';...
 'Validity checks: requested inverse-map residual, post-clip real-input mismatch, thrust and all three torque limits, Beta2 condition number and q/b3 denominator, tension and cable ellipsoid h at 25ms and four numerical substep endpoints. Synthetic motor dynamics, live EKF and full Flight switch are not simulated here; fixed 0.01kg is R193 EKF initial estimate only, true plant mass 0.14kg.';...
 'Static lint audited V37 bad ...]; pattern, new case configuration, 84-column trace row and name parity, and new coupling/temporal-audit schema. No MATLAB runtime available to run V38 in this environment; do not assert successful numerical convergence or safe collision avoidance.'};
add=[newline newline strjoin(notes,newline) newline];
v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'CBF_CUMULATIVE_HANDOVER_V38.txt'),[prior add]);
delete(p);
end


% =========================================================================
% V40: FAR ERROR, ORIGINAL-V19 BRANCHES, MATCHED TORQUES, VFD DERIVATIVES
