'1. 元Flight通常6階参照は固定。V19 R1再現の非退化実状態（t≈2.15s）またはFlightの連続状態履歴を初期化して、その後3〜4秒の連続閉ループを実行。簡単な人工的tilt状態ではなく実ログに基づく比較を優先。' ...
newline ...
'2. 4方式：元HLC、R1 thrust-only post、同じT要求を満たすmodified v1 full jet+Vs再計算+physically feasible torque、変更したv1とv2..4を共に最適化。原入力変更ΔT,Δτの作用をできるだけ揃え、入力ノルム・飽和・障害物h・張力・Intersample・追従誤差を同時判定。毎周期の仮想入力時間軌道とBeta2/Uf/alpha2対応残差を継続ログ。' ...
newline ...
'3. 元Vfdの高階列が実plant連続時間微分に等しいかを解析的なチェーンルール（実入力 u の依存を考慮）と小刻みdt比較で検査する。設計上『離散閉ループの予測列』であれば、連続微分系列と呼ばず区別。' ...
newline ...
'4. 上の条件で対応維持が有効なら仮想入力方式の実現可能集合・回避時の追従誤差管理を研究。飽和/不可行ならR1 4入力,R2 2段拡張,参照調整を比較。いずれも元安全幾何と物理張力条件を外さない。' ...
newline ...
'注意：コントローラ推定荷重0.01 kgは初期EKF固定、真値0.14 kgは物理plant。実Flight EKFとTakeoff/Flightモードを再現したとはみなさない。' ...
newline ...
'' ...
newline ...
'作業記録：V38ユーザZIPのCSVおよび原R193生成関数のread-only解析。新規MATLABソースを変更していない。元V38までの累積引継ぎバイト列はこの追加ファイルでそのまま保持。' ...
newline
];
notes={...
'===== V40 ADDENDUM: USER 10M/20M DISPLACEMENT, VFD CHAIN, EXACT V19 BRANCH AND MATCHED PHYSICAL TORQUE STUDY =====';...
'USER REQUIREMENTS: Original ordinary R193 Flight trajectory remains UNCHANGED and 6-times differentiable, with no special replan/C7 test; actual state may be 10 or 20 m from target. Compare baseline HLC, post-HLC thrust, generated v1 jet plus recomputed v234, and torque corrections in physical-domain matched amplitudes. Always propagate the nonlinear plant at 25ms ZOH and monitor actual saturation, cable safety and tension.';...
'V40 normal reference: ORIGINAL gen_ref_line + gen_ref_for_rigid_body(.pYaw,6); offsets apply only to physical payload pL(8:10), preserving cable direction/quaternion state manifold. A +10m z displacement is included; negative z offsets omitted because they can place a real load below ground, which is not currently a CBF constraint.';...
'V40 V19 branch: ORIGINAL V19 straight_single scenario and V11_19 dynamics, reconstruct exact R1 state at t=1.75 from t=0 and propagate multiple controls from that common state. The smooth v1 wave begins at this same t=1.75 with zero 0..5 derivatives and is continuously applied throughout the branch. The wave is NOT the actual R1 thrust trace or a safety-certified substitute. R1_EXACT is recomputed every 25ms and stops on infeasibility.';...
'V40 physical amplitude-match: V40_EQUAL_POST adds a direct pitch torque, V40_EQUAL_VIRTUAL uses independent smoothly varying deltaVs whose resulting torque increment has the SAME infinity norm at a common physical state after the same altered v1 map. Different torque direction makes long-run trajectories different. Same final physical u must always give same physical evolution; algebraic recoding alone cannot improve performance.';...
'VFD audit: original Vfd columns based on discrete F1 and vertical position/velocity error. Sweep epsilon time forward with a HELD physical input and actual R193/V19 plant to compare derivative of each column against claimed next column. For d0 analytic chain rule F1(1)*(zdot-vz)+F1(2)*(zddot-loadAz). The R193 derivative is approximated using a 1e-5s original nonlinear plant step, while V11 uses its vector field. This test is local, limited by differentiability/finite epsilon and does not derive higher Lie derivatives analytically.';...
'CBF design consequences: smooth reference alone does NOT guarantee feasibility or tracking from 10-20m error; require safe-set membership (h and derivatives), control authority and 4 physical input bounds, estimated load mass, positive tension, model domain, input time regularity, 25ms intersample safety and R1/R2 or virtual-input intervention feasibility. Max torque alone is insufficient.';...
'V40 source was statically inspected but NOT run inside MATLAB in assistant environment. Output statuses and numerical values must come from the user MATLAB ZIP before any claims of control improvement.'};
add=[newline newline v39 newline strjoin(notes,newline) newline];
v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'CBF_CUMULATIVE_HANDOVER_V40.txt'),[prior add]);
delete(p);
end

