 contains(prior,'V34 ADDENDUM') && contains(prior,'V33 ADDENDUM'),...
 'CBF:HLCV36HistoryMarkers','Some prior historical appendices are absent');
add=sprintf(['\n\n===== V36 ADDENDUM 2026-11-17: COMPLETE ORIGINAL-REFERENCE CLOSED-LOOP FIRST =====\n',...
 'V35 user result ZIP CBF_HLC_ROOTCAUSE_V35_20261117_134918_281.zip contains ONLY CBF_CUMULATIVE_HANDOVER_V34.txt (327375 UTF-8 bytes) and ERROR_TOP_LEVEL.txt. No simulated V35 traces were recorded. The error occurred in v35WriteHandover before flight simulation: MATLAB numel(prior)>250000 was wrong because UTF-8 bytes and decoded character counts were conflated. The file contains a V34 ADDENDUM. This was an administrative coding error, not an HLC control or plant error.\n',...
 'V36 removes the incorrect length threshold and checks the actual V32/V33/V34 historical markers. The entire original V35 handover and earlier history are generated from the same embedded source; append this V36 analysis rather than replacing it. History is written after the 25-ms closed-loop experiments. If handover formatting fails, preserve already computed CSVs and write an explicit warning.\n',...
 'Use ONLY the normal source R193 trajectory generated by gen_ref_line and gen_ref_for_rigid_body(.pYaw, 6th order); synthetic initial tilt, body roll, cable angular rate and lateral velocity are diagnostic physical-state perturbations, not user Flight measurements. No replanning or altered reference in the default case list.\n',...
 'Quick 9 cases/full 22 cases: NOMINAL, R1_EXACT, post-HLC changed thrust, changed v1 correction derivatives 0..4 re-inverted into original HLC physical input, direct 3-axis torque versus pointwise equivalent virtual Vs, and joint thrust/torque corrections. Run the SAME starting physical state in each case, retain raw and applied clipped inputs and all 25-ms samples, and 4 substep cable h and tension monitors.\n',...
 'For nondegenerate mapping effects set diagnostic initial q tilt, angular rate and body attitude; unlike prior V34 upright symmetry, v1 derivative columns can then act on lateral torques. This still is NOT the actual post-takeoff Flight estimated state. The estimated load mass is fixed 0.01 kg unless the user supplies live EKF mass history; true physical load is 0.14 kg.\n',...
 'PROOF LIMITS: pointwise virtual recoding of an unchanged physical 4-input vector cannot alter plant dynamics; changing v1 incremental 0..4 smoothly does not prove the original Vfd columns represent a continuous-time jet; 25-ms substep checks are not an intersample forward invariance guarantee. R1 t0 infeasibility is logged, not forced by relaxing safety. Saturation can break a proposed virtual input mapping.\n',...
 'Interpret from V33_CONTINUOUS_CASES_SUMMARY.csv, V35_PHYSICAL_STATE_V1_COLUMN_SENSITIVITY.csv, V33_TORQUE_PHYSICAL_EQUIVALENCE_AUDIT.csv and V35_V1_DERIVATIVE_CLOSED_LOOP_DIFFERENCES.csv (if generated). MATLAB runtime success of this new V36 build was not established in the assistant environment.\n',...
