 'V34 user ZIP quick=9 cases, full=22 cases on ORIGINAL R193 normal 6-derivative straight reference, diagnostic initial state, fixed EKF initial load estimate 0.01kg and true physical load 0.14kg. Every condition finished 6s except R1_EXACT, which stopped at t=0 with ZERO_INPUT_AUTHORITY_POSITIVE_RHS. No HLC computation crash. R1 did not apply an input, so the previously observed 135.229Nm V19 R1 event was NOT replayed in V34.\n',...
 'V34 FULL measurements: NOMINAL max raw |tau|=8.81e-16Nm, max position error=0.020063m, min cable h=-0.052893, negative h at 19 samples, first t=1.475s. POST_V1_T / V1_VALUE / V1_D1 / V1_D2 / V1_D3 / V1_JET have essentially identical applied 4D control and load states (max raw tau ~1e-15Nm), max position error=0.020063m; their min h=-0.046698. This is a DEGENERATE straight upright-cable case: q=[0,0,-1] and cable omega=0 stay invariant for thrust-only intervention. Hence one cannot infer that v1 higher derivatives are unnecessary; in the original V2_alpha2 they appear in terms involving transverse cable variables.\n',...
 'V34 FULL torque tests: +0.05Nm ROLL max raw tau=0.056838Nm, max load position error 0.264683m; PITCH=0.056838Nm and 0.198813m; YAW=0.055320Nm and 0.020063m. ROLL/PITCH/YAW post-HLC physical commands versus their virtual-vs pointwise recoding agree to numerical errors ~1.9e-9Nm max over full 241 timestamps; no change in the physical trajectory simply because of relabeling. All methods may have negative h near obstacle; NONE safety-certified.\n',...
 'V34 JOINT_DIRECT and JOINT_VIRTUAL_EQUIV are numerically identical; JOINT_NATIVE follows a DIFFERENT physical torque, so differences cannot establish a generic virtual design advantage. Physical map residual >100 belongs to comparing a deliberately different torque to the full-jet nominal alpha2, not a reported clipping event (zero clip cases).\n',...
 'The V34 pointwise V1 order audit shows identical 0..4 outputs at its upright initial state even when calculated smooth delta-v1 fourth derivative reaches ~1779. This verifies the scenario cannot excite the high-derivative transverse coupling, NOT that generated HLC ignores derivatives. The original generated Vfd returns a 6-component vertical v1 series. The R193 V2_alpha2 references dV1,d2V1,d3V1,d4V1.\n',...
 'V35 ONLY changes a controlled initial physical state (normal reference UNCHANGED): optional cable tilt in +Y, body roll, tangent cable angular velocity and lateral load velocity. Preserve q norm=1, q dot omega=0, quaternion unit. These are SYNTHETIC diagnosis states, not historical real Flight EKF states or implied reachable trajectories. 0 settings retain exact V34 baseline. Keep opts.continuousInitialState19 for actually measured source snapshots; cannot mix actual with synthetic adjustment.\n',...
 'V35 adds finite-difference sensitivity of the actual physical [T,tau] to each v1^(0..4) column at a common nondegenerate state, and full-loop derivative-order pair comparisons. These checks expose whether changed derivatives affect the HLC inverse and whether physical input limits can be met; they do not prove a time-consistent full HLC source derivative jet or a CBF safety theorem. Full-loop torque POST/VIRTUAL equality expected for same physical input.\n',...
 'IMPORTANT future goal: first compare nominal vs edited real physical inputs under the same initial q tilt / omega and NORMAL 6-jet reference; then formulate physically feasible virtual-input adjustment and real thrust/torque limits, including intersample safety and dynamic extension only where needed. For R1 zero authority at t0, report the geometric rectified coefficient, RHS and hR; changing reference does NOT cure R1 feasibility by assumption. Need actual Flight state and live EKF trajectory to make an apples-to-apples Flight verification.\n',...
 'No new MATLAB run claimed for V35; static source and algebraic finite-difference test logic inspected; V35 remains experiment, not certified safety controller.\n']);
v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'CBF_CUMULATIVE_HANDOVER_V35.txt'),[prior add]);
delete(p);
