 'Observed V33 failure: FAILED_CBF:HLCV32JetAudit at v32ReferenceAudit before continuous simulation. V33 ZIP V32_REFERENCE_0_TO_7_AUDIT.csv shows all normal R193 ORIGINAL derivatives 0..6 compare with themselves at zero error; optional synthetic C7_D_0.9 7th derivative at endpoint shows absolute floating point cancellation error 0.00018310546875 (6th 3.814697265625e-06). These are errors of the previously implemented power-basis evaluation at near-1 normalized time, NOT evidence of non-smooth normal Flight trajectory.' newline ...
 'User clarifies that the regular 6-derivative-smooth NORMAL trajectory, NOT a replanned/modified reference, is the experiment baseline. V34 therefore defaults opts.continuousSyntheticReference=false; standard quick has 9 all-ORIGINAL cases and full has 22 all-ORIGINAL cases. The unrelated C7 reference is not used or audited in standard runs. It can only be opted in explicitly for separate testing.' newline ...
 'The NORMAL reference comes directly from R193 source gen_ref_line p0=[0 0 3], velocity=1.5, direction=[0 1 0] and gen_ref_for_rigid_body(...,6). Independently audit [position; yaw] derivatives 0..6 against constant-speed closed-form, with payload Z shifted -cableLength at order 0 only. Original actual Flight runtime TAKEOFF/F stage, EKF state estimation, or replanning are NOT reproduced by this standalone flight-phase runner.' newline ...
 'Numerically stable S7: positive Bernstein degree-15 sum for k0 and derivative of 51480*s^7*(1-s)^7 with Leibniz rule for k1..7. S7 is used ONLY for smooth deliberate control-input diagnostic interventions, not to overwrite original Flight reference. Smooth-step self-audit is recorded but cannot block original flight simulation if it fails.' newline ...
 'Torque: Original-only full cases separately test roll/pitch/yaw positive and negative post-HLC corrections vs pointwise mapping through v2-v4, all at the same 25ms update and hard physical bounds. Same physical [T,taux,tauy,tauz] must yield the same next state; algebraic remapping cannot cure tracking/feedback errors. v1 input intervention compares post-HLC thrust-only, v1(d0), v1(d0..d1), ..., v1(d0..d4) with recomputed Beta2/alpha2 torque. Joint thrust+pitch corrections cover direct and virtual remap. Actual trace columns retain demanded, applied and clipping, h and tension including 4 step samples.' newline ...
 'STOP and report constraints: fixed 0.01kg is an explicitly tagged R193 initial EKF estimate, not current/live EKF; true plant load mass remains 0.14kg. 20N thrust and +/-1Nm torques are test assumptions not independently verified actuator ratings. Flight-phase initial state is constructed diagnostically unless actual snapshot opts.continuousInitialState19 provided. No R1/R2/virtual CBF success claimed. Cases can stop on infeasibility, tension or HLC domain; inspect per-case status and do not infer success from archive creation.' newline ...
 'No MATLAB R2026a interpreter is available to author. Static source/data checks and independent Python numeric S7 audits have been run; full user-side MATLAB execution remains to be confirmed.' newline];
v23WriteText(fullfile(work,'CBF_CUMULATIVE_HANDOVER_V34.txt'),[old add]);
