%|============================================================
%|V49 actual R1 data: z error -0.00371m, upward speed +0.361m/s at t=2.300; raw thrust +0.415N, applied thrust +13.502N, body thrust-axis tilt 5.58deg, cable tilt 4.17deg, raw torque 135.229Nm.
%|v1=F11*(zd-z)+F12*(vzd-vz) with F11 about 82.34, F12 about 24.83. At same state raw-thrust-zero vertical-velocity threshold is approx +0.383m/s at 2.300 and +0.347m/s at 2.325; measured speeds +0.361 and +0.489m/s respectively. These are time-varying algebraic zero-thrust thresholds, NOT allowable speed bounds nor CBF constraints.
%|Generated Beta2 depends on V1+target z acceleration+g. In V19 R1 the beta singular spectrum and Vs/alpha2 vary rapidly as raw thrust drops. A small condition number does not guarantee adequate absolute torque authority. At 2.300 sigmaMin about 4.949 and Vs norm about 657.
%|V51 retains original 6-derivative reference, original nonlinear plant, original R1 CBF and HLC with EKF initial mass 0.01kg held; it is NOT the real live EKF Flight loop.
%|V51 outputs exact R1 replay history, matched-state z/vz counterfactuals, algebraic v1-only authority sweep (higher v1 columns held fixed), and CURRENT-R1-constrained 25ms nonlinear 4-input one-step tests. Last two audits are NOT full-time coherent virtual CBF or certified forward invariant safety control.
%|Hypothesis: a small upward velocity can collapse original raw thrust while required R1 applied thrust remains high, and high-order Vs couples to reduced effective Beta2 control authority. Measure relative order of causation, distinguish algebraic from propagated interventions.
