%|[Most important new discovery: beta2 singularity at zero nominal thrust]
%|V51_SAME_STATE_V1_BETA_ALPHA_SWEEP: at each t=2.150,2.225,2.275,2.300,2.325 the root v1 in approximately [-9.808,-9.806] results in computed HLC raw T approx 0 and beta2 sigmaMin approx 0, i.e., beta2 inversion is singular/degenerate there. This is an algebraic same-state scan with higher v1 derivative columns held frozen; NOT a realizable continuous-time corrected v1 jet.
