%|2. Fundamental distinctions for the user's new question
%|(a) pointwise algebraic consistency: given x and invertible mapping, replacing the physical control by a virtual command consistent with the SAME physical u does not change the plant response at all. Renaming/reparameterizing a control is not a new stabilizing intervention. In the generated HLC, T=Uf(x,ref,v1) and tau=Beta2(x,ref,v1)^{-1} V2_alpha2(x,ref,v1-jets,vs). If T changes, re-evaluate Uf, Beta2, V2_alpha2; do NOT keep beta/alpha frozen from original v1. If beta/alpha are well-defined and affine in virtual variables, algebraic inverse can be checked with forward reconstruction residual.
%|(b) jet/time consistency: v1, dv1, d2v1, d3v1, d4v1 are NOT five independent control variables without extra dynamics. A time-varying changed v1(t) must have derivatives consistent with its evolution; changing only v1 in each 25ms sample and holding higher jets from old reference is pointwise but NOT dynamically consistent. Smoothness and slew constraints; new HLC inversion must respect thrust and torque hard boxes with no silent saturation.
%|(c) reference/error consistency: even perfect inversion of a modified virtual input forces a NEW output behavior. The original trajectory may become temporarily unreachable. The unchanged high-gain HLC feedback can demand huge actions, or the actuator box/safety set may make commands infeasible; algebraic consistency alone does not prevent this.
%|(d) actual plant/sensor consistency: controller estimated load mhat, plant true mL, physical actuation, sample-and-hold and state estimates differ. A virtual inverse constructed with mhat need not produce the claimed output derivative in true plant. Match and verify this residual in original 3D plant with and without EKF, not an invented EKF value.
%|
%|3. Priority test matrix (same plant/trajectory/initial states/mhat/input limits)
%|A NOMINAL: raw HLC then physical clipping, log before/after.
%|B R1_DIRECT: genuine R1 CBF recomputed each 25ms, physical thrust corrected, torque nominal/clipped (V19/V28 reproduction).
%|C R1_REINVERT_POINTWISE: choose R1's same thrust correction; invert Uf with a modified v1 and recompute Vs, Beta2, V2_alpha2 and physical torques at same state. Hold higher v1 jets nominal ONLY as an intentionally labeled algebraic diagnostic; verify input bounds and residual; not an honest dynamically consistent virtual controller and not safe automatically.
%|D R1_VIRTUAL_JET_CONSISTENT: use a realizable, differentiable virtual command/jet, project through exact generated HLC, enforce actual T/tau limits; reconstruct & verify derivative coherence at successive 25ms steps and one-step physical plant. If no feasible candidate, STOP_INFEASIBLE; never clip and label it mapping-consistent.
%|E SAME_PHYSICAL_INPUT_DIFFERENT_DESCRIPTION (null test): physical u exactly B, only calculate equivalent virtual representation; state trajectory and HLC outputs must match B to solver/integrator tolerance. This confirms algebraic relabeling alone cannot improve behavior.
%|F TORQUE_ONLY and THRUST_ONLY and JOINT: single-step and sustained interventions, equal matched magnitude/limits, compare virtual residual/closed loop.
%|G WITH_VS_WITHOUT_VS_OUTER_FEEDBACK: diagnostic gain term cancellation at fixed state, NOT an approved alternate flight controller or 'gain tuning success'. Need causal comparison of second derivative tracking errors, derivative levels, and cancellation.
%|H SATURATION_ONLY: branch at 2.275s into physical tau box and artificially unbounded torque for 25/50ms, label the unbounded run NONPHYSICAL, to isolate saturation as cause/amplifier. Never count nonphysical case as avoidance success.
%|I MASS & MODEL: mhat=0.01 initial replay separately from live EKF estimates; true plant mL=0.14 only plant; 19-state vs original 24-state parity, high-order derivative consistency; no oracle mass in controller.
%|J INTERSAMPLE & HARD CONSTRAINTS: preserve cable ellipsoid h, all physical input bounds, positive cable tension, sample/hold 25ms plus substeps; record CBF residual and feasibility, do NOT silence failed safety rows.
%|
%|4. Metrics & interpretation
%|Log rawHLC 4 inputs, clipped nominal, proposed CBF, finally applied, achieved next state, HLC fully reconstructed tau, Uf residual, beta/alpha, singular values, D=qz(q.b3), pL position/velocity error, reconstructed x-horizontal acceleration and jerk errors, Vs14 signed terms and cancellations; actual-vs-desired virtual-output derivative (if mathematically defined for the model), derivative/jet time consistency, mhat and true mass separated, hard-box feasibility, h and continuous sample approximations, cable tension at actually propagated steps; solver status/time.
%|Report the earliest time when each event happens: intervention, derivative mismatch, first Vs surge, raw torque > physical box, actual torque clipping, HLC map condition warning, CBF infeasible, physical h violation. Differentiate algebraic exactness, causal paired test, and invariant safety proof. A large number in virtual mapping may be FEASIBILITY failure even if cable h remains positive.
%|
%|5. Literature touchpoints (not model-specific guarantees)
%|Convens et al., IFAC-PapersOnLine 2017, Control of Fully Actuated Unmanned Aerial Vehicles with Actuator Saturation (feedback linearization, actuator saturation, reference governor), DOI 10.1016/j.ifacol.2017.08.1823.
%|Design of shifting state-feedback controllers for constrained feedback linearized systems: Application to quadrotor attitude control, International Journal of Robust and Nonlinear Control (2023) DOI 10.1002/rnc.7098: physical constraints mapped into the virtual-input domain.
%|These works are not directly applicable proofs for the present cable-suspended drone; refer to exact generated HLC and 3D plant.
