%|============================================================
%|V51 2026-11-17: HLC validity mechanism (thrust and torque, not arbitrary caps)
%|============================================================
%|V49 actual R1 data: z error -0.00371m, upward speed +0.361m/s at t=2.300; raw thrust +0.415N, applied thrust +13.502N, body thrust-axis tilt 5.58deg, cable tilt 4.17deg, raw torque 135.229Nm.
%|v1=F11*(zd-z)+F12*(vzd-vz) with F11 about 82.34, F12 about 24.83. At same state raw-thrust-zero vertical-velocity threshold is approx +0.383m/s at 2.300 and +0.347m/s at 2.325; measured speeds +0.361 and +0.489m/s respectively. These are time-varying algebraic zero-thrust thresholds, NOT allowable speed bounds nor CBF constraints.
